{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Jacob stole the heart of Laban.</b> He did not let him perceive at all that he took notice of the evil speech Laban had directed against him, or that his countenance toward Jacob was not as it had been formerly." "<b>The Aramean.</b> He did this because Laban was an Aramean, a man of deceit, so that if Laban had perceived that Jacob was aware of this, he would have tracked his every step and Jacob would have had no way to escape." "<b>In that he did not tell him.</b> Like עַל עֹלַת הַתָּמִיד (Numbers 28:10). Jacob presented himself as though unaware of Laban's hostility, aside from simply not telling him that he intended to leave. All this he did not from lack of moral discipline but as a necessity, for he was fleeing, out of fear that Laban would despoil him with the help of his townsmen, as he says in his defense to Laban afterward."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:46.558002622Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}